-- title:
--   Integer weighted travel through endpoint events
-- statement:
--   For a list of events on a positive cycle, a directed move from the first endpoint of an event to the second has weight equal to their forward cyclic distance, read as an integer. The reverse move has the negative of that same distance. Travel is the relation generated by zero length travel at each vertex and concatenation of moves, adding weights. Repetition of edges is allowed. Also define a head shift giving value $v$ at position zero, $-v$ at position $v$, and zero elsewhere, checking zero first. Travel retains signed integer displacement rather than reducing its total modulo the cycle length.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/ZeroGapEventTravel.lean#L10-L47

